            "text": "Credit is, in its simplest form, a measure of trust. It is the financial system's method of evaluating whether you can be relied upon to repay borrowed money. Every time you apply for a loan, sign a lease, or open a credit card, the institution on the other side of that transaction asks one fundamental question: based on this person's history, what is the probability that they will pay us back?"
